# =============================================================
# AI tooling — never tracked, never shipped.
# Covers Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Aider, Gemini, Continue,
# Codeium, Windsurf, Zed AI, OpenHands, Tabnine, and any
# convention-named project-instruction file (CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md,
# COPILOT.md, AGENTS.md, etc.). If a new tool drops a config
# directory or a per-project instruction file in the repo root,
# add it here rather than letting it leak into a public push.
# =============================================================
.claude/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.cursorignore
.aider*
.windsurfrules
.windsurf/
.continue/
.codeium*
.tabnine/
.openhands/
.gemini/
.cody/
.zed/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/instructions/
agent-skills/

# Per-project AI-assistant instruction files. Not project source.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
GEMINI.md
COPILOT.md
AGENTS.md
AGENT.md
AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md
.aiderules

# Internal session work and dated session recaps. Useful for the
# original developer's continuity, not for public consumers.
.archive/
docs/session_recap_*.md

# NES ROMs are user-supplied. Never ship a commercial ROM.
#
# Keep this as `roms/*`, not `roms/`. Git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so excluding `roms/` makes every negation below unreachable and
# the nestest artifacts silently fail to ship. Excluding the entries instead
# leaves the directory walkable, so a negation can re-include one child.
# Check with: git check-ignore -v roms/.test_roms/nestest.nes   (must not match)
roms/*

# Homebrew CPU validation artifacts (kevtris's nestest and its Nintendulator
# golden trace), tracked despite the roms/* and *.log globs above so the
# nestest gate runs on a fresh clone with no download step. Provenance and
# redistribution terms: roms/.test_roms/PROVENANCE.md.
!roms/.test_roms/
!roms/.test_roms/*

# Library scan output (large, machine-generated, regenerable via
# scripts/playability_sweep.py and scripts/parity_sweep.py).
parity_sweep.json
playability_sweep*.json

third_party/
tests/parity/mesen_tapes/*.status.txt
demos/

# PGO transient instrumentation dumps — only the merged nes_core.profdata is tracked
nes_core/pgo/raw/
# Local experiment artifacts (archives, handoffs, receipts, demos) — large,
# regenerable, referenced by path from configs; never committed.
runs/
